<article class="env-lemma" id="0FCX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FCX">Lemma <span data-tag="0FCX">23.10.2</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a flat finite type ring map of Noetherian rings. If </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  B \otimes _ A B \longrightarrow B  \]
</div>
  <p> is a perfect ring map, i.e., if $B$ has finite tor dimension over $B \otimes _ A B$, then $B$ is a smooth $A$-algebra. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0FCW" data-tag="0FCW">23.10.1</a> and general facts about smooth ring maps, see Algebra, Lemmas <a href="/tag/07BU" data-tag="07BU">10.137.11</a> and <a href="/tag/00TC" data-tag="00TC">10.137.12</a>. Alternatively, the reader can slightly modify the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0FCW" data-tag="0FCW">23.10.1</a> to prove this lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>